IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part1-preliminary`

-- scja1-part3-div5-6.l4: Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- LAYER 1, Part 3, Division 5 "Supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction" (ss 23 to 28) and Division 6 "Allocation of proceedings" (ss 28A, 28B). s 28B is shown repealed.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering, not the official text. Every name begins with the section it implements. Imports the keel's `scja-core` and this part's s 2 module (for "subordinate court").
-- A judgment the text leaves to the court or the Chief Justice ("desirable in the interests of justice", "necessary or expedient", "seem necessary to secure that substantial justice is done") is a plain input.

§ `Part 3: General Division of High Court (continued)`

§§ `Division 5: Supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction`

§§§ `Section 23: Revision of criminal proceedings of subordinate courts`

-- Plain gloss: may the General Division exercise powers of revision in these criminal proceedings in a subordinate court? In accordance with the written law on criminal procedure.
-- src:1886 | 23. The General Division may exercise powers of revision in
-- src:1888 | respect of criminal proceedings and matters in subordinate courts in
-- src:1895 | accordance with the provisions of any written law for the time being
-- src:1896 | in force relating to criminal procedure.
@ref s 23 (src:1886-1896)
GIVEN `lower court` IS A Court @desc Which court or tribunal are the criminal proceedings or matters in?
      `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law give a right of appeal from this body's decisions to the Supreme Court?
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding` @desc Are the proceedings criminal, quasi-criminal or civil?
      `the powers are exercised in accordance with the written law relating to criminal procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the powers of revision exercised in accordance with the provisions of any written law for the time being in force relating to criminal procedure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `lower court` `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "criminal proceedings and matters in subordinate courts"
        IF `s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `lower court` `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the body is a subordinate court is not decided by s 2
        IF NOT (nature EQUALS `a criminal proceeding`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "criminal proceedings and matters"
        IF `the powers are exercised in accordance with the written law relating to criminal procedure` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with the provisions of any written law for the time being in force relating to criminal procedure"

§§§ `Section 24: Power of General Division to call for records of civil proceedings in subordinate courts`

-- Plain gloss: may the General Division call for and examine the record of these civil proceedings in a subordinate court? For the purpose of satisfying itself as to the correctness, legality or propriety of a
-- decision, or the regularity of the proceedings.
-- src:1903 | 24. The General Division may call for and examine the record of
-- src:1904 | any civil proceedings before any subordinate court for the purpose of
-- src:1905 | satisfying itself as to the correctness, legality or propriety of any
-- src:1906 | decision recorded or passed, and as to the regularity of any
-- src:1907 | proceedings of any such subordinate court.
@ref s 24 (src:1903-1907)
GIVEN `lower court` IS A Court
      `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
      `the purpose is to satisfy itself as to the correctness, legality or propriety of a decision, or the regularity of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to satisfy the General Division as to the correctness, legality or propriety of any decision recorded or passed, or as to the regularity of any proceedings of the subordinate court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24 the General Division may call for and examine the record of the civil proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `lower court` `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any civil proceedings before any subordinate court"
        IF `s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `lower court` `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the body is a subordinate court is not decided by s 2
        IF NOT (nature EQUALS `a civil proceeding`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any civil proceedings"
        IF `the purpose is to satisfy itself as to the correctness, legality or propriety of a decision, or the regularity of the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of satisfying itself as to the correctness, legality or propriety of any decision ... and as to the regularity of any proceedings"

§§§ `Section 25: Powers of General Division on revision of civil proceedings`

-- Plain gloss: may the General Division give such orders on these civil proceedings in a subordinate court, including directing a new trial? Where the record has been called for, or has otherwise come to its
-- knowledge, and the orders seem necessary to secure that substantial justice is done.
-- src:1913 | 25. In the case of any civil proceedings in a subordinate court the
-- src:1914 | record of which has been called for, or which otherwise comes to its
-- src:1915 | knowledge, the General Division may give such orders thereon,
-- src:1916 | either by directing a new trial or otherwise, as seem necessary to
-- src:1917 | secure that substantial justice is done.
@ref s 25 (src:1913-1917)
GIVEN `lower court` IS A Court
      `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
      `the record has been called for, or the proceedings have otherwise come to the knowledge of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division called for the record, or have the proceedings otherwise come to its knowledge?
      `the orders seem necessary to secure that substantial justice is done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the orders seem necessary to secure that substantial justice is done?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25 the General Division may give such orders on the civil proceedings, including directing a new trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `lower court` `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any civil proceedings in a subordinate court"
        IF `s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `lower court` `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the body is a subordinate court is not decided by s 2
        IF NOT (nature EQUALS `a civil proceeding`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any civil proceedings"
        IF NOT `the record has been called for, or the proceedings have otherwise come to the knowledge of the General Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the record of which has been called for, or which otherwise comes to its knowledge"
        IF `the orders seem necessary to secure that substantial justice is done` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such orders ... as seem necessary to secure that substantial justice is done"

§§§ `Section 26: No revision at instance of party who could have appealed`

-- Plain gloss: does s 26 apply to this revision proceeding, so that it cannot be entertained? "Where an appeal lies from any decision in any civil matter, and no appeal is brought": a "where" not met
-- is a no for the section (the twin). The party must be one "who could have appealed".
-- src:1923 | 26. Where an appeal lies from any decision in any civil matter, and
-- src:1924 | no appeal is brought, no proceeding by way of revision is to be
-- src:1925 | entertained at the instance of a party who could have appealed.
@ref s 26 (src:1923-1925)
GIVEN `an appeal lies from the decision in the civil matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an appeal lie from the decision in the civil matter?
      `no appeal is brought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no appeal been brought?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 the section applies to the civil matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an appeal lies from the decision in the civil matter` AND `no appeal is brought` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an appeal lies from any decision in any civil matter, and no appeal is brought"

@ref s 26 no proceeding by way of revision is to be entertained (src:1923-1925)
GIVEN `an appeal lies from the decision in the civil matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no appeal is brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is a party who could have appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party who could have appealed against the decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 a proceeding by way of revision may be entertained at the instance of the party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 26 the section applies to the civil matter` `an appeal lies from the decision in the civil matter` `no appeal is brought` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the party is a party who could have appealed` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no proceeding by way of revision is to be entertained at the instance of a party who could have appealed"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the instance of a party who could have appealed"; the section grants nothing

§§§ `Section 27: General supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction of General Division`

-- s 27(1). Plain gloss: does the General Division have general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction over this court? Over all subordinate courts; a body that s 2 does not make a subordinate court is
-- outside the sentence.
-- src:1930 | 27.—(1) In addition to the powers conferred on the General
-- src:1931 | Division by this Act or any other written law, the General Division
-- src:1932 | has general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction over all
-- src:1933 | subordinate courts.
@ref s 27(1) (src:1930-1933)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) the General Division has general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction over the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` court `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "over all subordinate courts"

-- The three things s 27(2) lets the General Division do.
DECLARE `s 27(2) step` IS ONE OF
    `s 27(2) calls for the record`
    `s 27(2) removes the matter or proceeding into the General Division`
    `s 27(2) gives the subordinate court directions as to the further conduct of the matter or proceeding`

-- s 27(2). Plain gloss: may the General Division take this step in a matter or proceeding, civil or criminal, in a subordinate court? "if it appears desirable in the interests of justice": a condition
-- (met, the power; not met, the text's no for this subsection). Of its own motion or at the instance of any party or person interested, at any stage.
-- src:1937 | (2) The General Division may in particular, but without limiting
-- src:1938 | subsection (1), if it appears desirable in the interests of justice, either
-- src:1939 | of its own motion or at the instance of any party or person interested,
-- src:1940 | at any stage in any matter or proceeding, whether civil or criminal, in
-- src:1941 | any subordinate court, call for the record thereof, and may remove the
-- src:1948 | matter or proceeding into the General Division or may give to the
-- src:1949 | subordinate court such directions as to the further conduct of the
-- src:1950 | matter or proceeding as justice may require.
@ref s 27(2) (src:1937-1950)
GIVEN step IS A `s 27(2) step` @desc Which step: calling for the record, removing the matter or proceeding into the General Division, or giving the subordinate court directions as to its further conduct?
      court IS A Court
      `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears desirable in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear desirable in the interests of justice to take the step?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) the General Division may take the step in the matter or proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` court `a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any subordinate court"
        IF `it appears desirable in the interests of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it appears desirable in the interests of justice"

-- s 27(3). Upon the General Division calling for a record under (2), all proceedings in the subordinate court in the matter are stayed pending further order of the General Division. "Upon": not called is
-- a no; "pending further order": a further order lifts the stay (the bar is encoded; the further order's content is not).
-- src:1954 | (3) Upon the General Division calling for any record under
-- src:1955 | subsection (2), all proceedings in the subordinate court in the
-- src:1956 | matter or proceeding in question are to be stayed pending further
-- src:1957 | order of the General Division.
@ref s 27(3) (src:1954-1957)
GIVEN `the General Division has called for the record under section 27(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division called for the record under section 27(2)?
      `the General Division has made a further order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division made a further order in the matter or proceeding?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(3) the proceedings in the subordinate court are stayed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the General Division has called for the record under section 27(2)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the General Division calling for any record under subsection (2)"
        IF `the General Division has made a further order` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "pending further order of the General Division"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 27(4). The General Division, when exercising (or deciding whether to exercise) its jurisdiction under (1) or powers under (2) in relation to a matter that concerns a case where it has heard and determined
-- an appeal from a subordinate court, is to have regard to whether the matter was, or could reasonably have been, raised in that appeal. A "when" not met is a no for the section.
-- src:1961 | (4) The General Division, when exercising (or deciding whether to
-- src:1962 | exercise) its supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction under
-- src:1963 | subsection (1) or powers under subsection (2) in relation to any
-- src:1964 | matter which concerns a case where the General Division has heard
-- src:1965 | and determined an appeal from a subordinate court, is to have regard
-- src:1966 | to whether that matter was, or could reasonably have been, raised in
-- src:1967 | that appeal.
@ref s 27(4) (src:1961-1967)
GIVEN `the General Division is exercising, or deciding whether to exercise, its jurisdiction under section 27(1) or powers under section 27(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division exercising, or deciding whether to exercise, its supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction under section 27(1) or powers under section 27(2)?
      `the matter concerns a case where the General Division has heard and determined an appeal from a subordinate court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter concern a case where the General Division has heard and determined an appeal from a subordinate court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(4) the General Division is to have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the General Division is exercising, or deciding whether to exercise, its jurisdiction under section 27(1) or powers under section 27(2)` AND `the matter concerns a case where the General Division has heard and determined an appeal from a subordinate court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when exercising (or deciding whether to exercise) ... in relation to any matter which concerns a case where the General Division has heard and determined an appeal from a subordinate court"

-- s 27(4) as a regulative rule (ruling N2: derived from the decision above). The bearer is "the General Division"; no time is stated.
DECLARE `s 27(4) party` IS ONE OF `s 27(4) the General Division`
DECLARE `s 27(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 27(4) has regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal`
    `s 27(4) decides without having that regard`

@ref s 27(4) is to have regard (src:1961-1967)
GIVEN `the General Division is exercising, or deciding whether to exercise, its jurisdiction under section 27(1) or powers under section 27(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter concerns a case where the General Division has heard and determined an appeal from a subordinate court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 27(4) party` `s 27(4) act`
`s 27(4) the General Division must have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` MEANS
    IF `s 27(4) the General Division is to have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` `the General Division is exercising, or deciding whether to exercise, its jurisdiction under section 27(1) or powers under section 27(2)` `the matter concerns a case where the General Division has heard and determined an appeal from a subordinate court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `s 27(4) the General Division`
         MUST `s 27(4) has regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 27(4): the General Division is to have regard to whether the matter was, or could reasonably have been, raised in the appeal"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Section 28: Discretion of General Division as to hearing parties`

-- s 28(1). Subject to the provisions of any written law, no party has any right to be heard before the General Division when it exercises its powers of supervision and revision. A written law that gives the
-- right takes the question out of this subsection (NOTHING).
-- src:1973 | 28.—(1) Subject to the provisions of any written law for the time
-- src:1974 | being in force, no party has any right to be heard before the General
-- src:1975 | Division when exercising its powers of supervision and revision.
@ref s 28(1) (src:1973-1975)
GIVEN `the General Division is exercising its powers of supervision and revision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division exercising its powers of supervision and revision?
      `a written law gives the party a right to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law give the party a right to be heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) the party has a right to be heard before the General Division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the General Division is exercising its powers of supervision and revision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when exercising its powers of supervision and revision"
        IF `a written law gives the party a right to be heard` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to the provisions of any written law for the time being in force"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no party has any right to be heard before the General Division"

-- s 28(2). No final order may be made to the prejudice of any person unless that person has had an opportunity of being so heard. The function below asks the grant ("may the order be made"): "unless" met lifts the bar and the subsection grants nothing itself, so it answers NOTHING (fork F16); the twin after it asks the bar.
-- src:1979 | (2) No final order may be made to the prejudice of any person
-- src:1980 | unless that person has had an opportunity of being so heard.
@ref s 28(2) (src:1979-1980)
GIVEN `the order is a final order made to the prejudice of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a final order made to the prejudice of the person?
      `the person has had an opportunity of being heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person had an opportunity of being heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) the final order may be made to the prejudice of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order is a final order made to the prejudice of the person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No final order may be made to the prejudice of any person"
        IF `the person has had an opportunity of being heard` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless that person has had an opportunity of being so heard" lifts the bar; the subsection grants nothing itself
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No final order may be made to the prejudice of any person unless that person has had an opportunity of being so heard"

-- s 28(2), the twin for the bar: does the bar on a final order made to the prejudice of the person apply? JUST TRUE if the order is a final order to the person's prejudice and the person has not been heard; JUST FALSE once the "unless" is met; NOTHING for an order that is not a final order to the person's prejudice.
@ref s 28(2) the bar applies (src:1979-1980)
GIVEN `the order is a final order made to the prejudice of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has had an opportunity of being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) the bar on a final order made to the prejudice of the person applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order is a final order made to the prejudice of the person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No final order may be made to the prejudice of any person"
        IF `the person has had an opportunity of being heard` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that person has had an opportunity of being so heard"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Division 6: Allocation of proceedings`

-- s 28B is shown "[Repealed by Act 40 of 2019]": nothing to encode (coverage table: repealed or blank in this text).

§§§ `Section 28A: Allocation of proceedings to District Court or Family Court`

-- s 28A(1). Plain gloss: may the Chief Justice by order direct a class of proceedings commenced in the General Division to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court? "where he or she considers
-- it necessary or expedient to improve efficiency in the administration of justice and to provide for more speedy disposal": a "where" not met is a no for the subsection.
-- src:1988 | 28A.—(1) The Chief Justice may, where he or she considers it
-- src:1989 | necessary or expedient to improve efficiency in the administration of
-- src:1990 | justice and to provide for more speedy disposal of proceedings
-- src:1991 | commenced in the General Division, by order direct such class or
-- src:1992 | classes or description of proceedings as may be specified in the order
-- src:1993 | to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court.
@ref s 28A(1) (src:1988-1993)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice considers it necessary or expedient to improve efficiency in the administration of justice and to provide for more speedy disposal of proceedings commenced in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Chief Justice consider it necessary or expedient to improve efficiency in the administration of justice and to provide for more speedy disposal of proceedings commenced in the General Division?
      `the direction is made by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the direction made by an order?
      `the court that is to hear and determine the class of proceedings` IS A Court @desc Which court is the class of proceedings to be heard and determined by: the District Court, the Family Court, or another?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28A(1) the Chief Justice may by order direct the class of proceedings to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the court that is to hear and determine the class of proceedings` EQUALS `District Court` OR `the court that is to hear and determine the class of proceedings` EQUALS `Family Court`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court" names two courts with no "only"; a direction to another court, such as a Magistrate's Court, is not decided (fork F17)
        IF `the Chief Justice considers it necessary or expedient to improve efficiency in the administration of justice and to provide for more speedy disposal of proceedings commenced in the General Division` AND `the direction is made by order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where he or she considers it necessary or expedient to improve efficiency"

-- The five things s 28A(2) says an order under (1) may do.
DECLARE `s 28A(2) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 28A(2)(a)(i) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings it would lack only because the amount exceeds its monetary limit`
    `s 28A(2)(a)(ii) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings relating to a matter in section 17(1)(b) or (c)`
    `s 28A(2)(aa) confer jurisdiction on a Family Court over proceedings it would not otherwise have jurisdiction to hear and determine`
    `s 28A(2)(b) make provision governing appeals relating to proceedings transferred, including restricting the right of appeal`
    `s 28A(2)(c) make incidental provision for the transfer of the proceedings, including procedure and costs`

-- s 28A(2). Plain gloss: may an order under (1) make this provision? "Despite any other written law", the order "may" do each of (a)(i), (a)(ii), (aa), (b), (c). The paragraphs are named and there is no "only", so any
-- other provision is not decided (NOTHING). (a)(ii)'s "matters referred to in section 17(1)(b) or (c)" are admiralty or shipping, bankruptcy and companies (s 17(1)(b), (c) as encoded in scja1-part3-div2-jurisdiction).
-- src:2002 | (2) Despite any other written law, any order under subsection (1) —
-- src:2004 | (a) may confer jurisdiction on a District Court to hear and
-- src:2005 | determine —
-- src:2007 | (i) any proceedings specified in the order which, but for
-- src:2008 | the order, the District Court would not have
-- src:2009 | jurisdiction to hear and determine by reason only
-- src:2010 | of the fact that the amount involved exceeds the
-- src:2011 | monetary limit of its jurisdiction; or
-- src:2013 | (ii) any proceedings relating to any of the matters
-- src:2014 | referred to in section 17(1)(b) or (c);
-- src:2016 | (aa) may confer jurisdiction on a Family Court to hear and
-- src:2017 | determine any proceedings specified in the order which,
-- src:2018 | but for the order, the Family Court would not have
-- src:2019 | jurisdiction to hear and determine;
-- src:2021 | (b) may make such provision governing appeals relating to
-- src:2022 | proceedings transferred to the District Court or Family
-- src:2023 | Court (including provisions restricting the right of appeal)
-- src:2024 | as the Chief Justice thinks fit; and
-- src:2026 | (c) may make such incidental provision for the transfer of the
-- src:2027 | proceedings to the District Court or Family Court
-- src:2028 | (including matters relating to procedure and costs) as the
-- src:2029 | Chief Justice thinks fit.
@ref s 28A(2) (src:2002-2029)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 28A(2) provision` @desc Which provision: conferring jurisdiction on a District Court where only the amount exceeds its limit, conferring jurisdiction on a District Court over a matter in section 17(1)(b) or (c), conferring jurisdiction on a Family Court, governing appeals, or incidental transfer provision?
      `the order is made under section 28A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under section 28A(1)?
      subject IS A `Subject of the case` @desc For a District Court: what is the proceeding about?
      `the District Court would lack jurisdiction by reason only that the amount exceeds its monetary limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the District Court lack jurisdiction by reason only of the fact that the amount involved exceeds the monetary limit of its jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order is made under section 28A(1)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any order under subsection (1)"
        IF provision EQUALS `s 28A(2)(a)(i) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings it would lack only because the amount exceeds its monetary limit`
           AND `the District Court would lack jurisdiction by reason only that the amount exceeds its monetary limit` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)(i)
        IF provision EQUALS `s 28A(2)(a)(ii) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings relating to a matter in section 17(1)(b) or (c)`
           AND (subject EQUALS `admiralty or shipping` OR subject EQUALS bankruptcy OR subject EQUALS companies) THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)(ii)
        IF provision EQUALS `s 28A(2)(aa) confer jurisdiction on a Family Court over proceedings it would not otherwise have jurisdiction to hear and determine` THEN JUST TRUE -- (aa)
        IF provision EQUALS `s 28A(2)(b) make provision governing appeals relating to proceedings transferred, including restricting the right of appeal` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        IF provision EQUALS `s 28A(2)(c) make incidental provision for the transfer of the proceedings, including procedure and costs` THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) is for the proceedings it names; the paragraphs have no "only"
